.TH XTRACER_CLI 1 "March 2026" UNIX "User Manuals"
.SH NAME
xtracer_cli \- command-line renderer for XTRACER scenes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xtracer_cli
[
.I options
]
.I scene.scn
.br
.B xtracer_cli
.B version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xtracer_cli
loads a
.B .scn
scene file, renders it with the selected integrator, and writes a tonemapped PNG image.
.PP
Default output filename:
.I <scene_basename>_<renderer>.png
.SH OPTIONS
.IP "\fB-renderer\fR \fIname\fR"
Integrator to use.
Default: \fBpathtracer\fR.
.IP "\fB-res\fR \fI<width>x<height>\fR"
Framebuffer resolution.
Default: \fB640x480\fR.
.IP "\fB-rdepth\fR \fIuint\fR"
Maximum ray recursion depth.
Default: \fB3\fR.
.IP "\fB-samples\fR \fIuint\fR"
Sample count.
Must be 1 or greater.
Default: \fB1\fR.
.IP "\fB-aa\fR \fIuint\fR"
Supersampling anti-aliasing level.
Must be 2 or greater when provided.
Default: \fB1\fR.
.IP "\fB-tile_size\fR \fIuint\fR"
Tile width/height in pixels.
.IP "\fB-threads\fR \fIuint\fR"
Worker thread count.
\fB0\fR lets the runtime choose automatically.
Default: \fB0\fR.
.IP "\fB-cam\fR \fIname\fR"
Active camera name.
If omitted, the first camera in the scene is used.
.IP "\fB-outdir\fR \fIpath\fR"
Output directory for exported PNG.
.IP "\fB-mod\fR \fIexpression\fR"
Apply scene modifier. May be repeated.
.IP "\fBversion\fR"
Print version and exit.
Note: this form is positional (\fBversion\fR), not \fB-version\fR.
.SH RENDERERS
Known renderer IDs:
.IP "\fBraytracer\fR"
Whitted-style ray tracer.
.IP "\fBpathtracer\fR"
Brute-force path tracer.
.IP "\fBpathtracer_mis\fR, \fBpathtracer_is\fR"
MIS diffuse path tracer aliases.
.IP "\fBpathtracer_mis_full\fR"
Full MIS path tracer.
.IP "\fBphoton_mapping\fR"
Photon mapping.
.IP "\fBao\fR"
Ambient occlusion.
.IP "\fBdebug_views\fR"
Debug view integrator.
.IP "\fBdepth\fR, \fBstencil\fR, \fBnormal\fR, \fBuv\fR, \fBemission\fR"
Debug view aliases.
.SH SCENE AUTHORING GUIDE
XTRACER scene files use a simple key/group format.
Top-level sections commonly include:
.IP "\(bu"
\fBtitle\fR, \fBdescription\fR, \fBversion\fR, \fBdefault_camera\fR
.IP "\(bu"
\fBenvironment\fR, \fBcamera\fR, \fBgeometry\fR, \fBmaterial\fR, \fBobject\fR
.IP "\(bu"
optional \fBvariants\fR overlays
.PP
Minimal scene template:
.PP
.EX
title = Minimal Scene
description = Small starter scene
version = 1.0
default_camera = cam_main

environment = {
  type = color
  config = { value = col3(0.05,0.05,0.05) }
}

camera = {
  cam_main = {
    type = thin-lens
    fov = 45
    position = vec3(0,1,-5)
    target = vec3(0,0,0)
    up = vec3(0,1,0)
  }
}

geometry = {
  g_sphere = { type = sphere, position = vec3(0,0,0), radius = 1 }
}

material = {
  m_lambert = {
    type = lambert
    properties = {
      samplers = {
        diffuse = { type = color, value = col3(0.8,0.2,0.2) }
      }
    }
  }
}

object = {
  sphere = { geometry = g_sphere, material = m_lambert }
}
.EE
.PP
Common values:
.IP "\(bu"
Environment \fBtype\fR: \fBgradient\fR, \fBcolor\fR, \fBcubemap\fR, \fBerp\fR
.IP "\(bu"
Camera \fBtype\fR: \fBthin-lens\fR, \fBods\fR, \fBerp\fR, \fBcubemap\fR
.IP "\(bu"
Geometry \fBtype\fR: \fBplane\fR, \fBsphere\fR, \fBpoint\fR, \fBtriangle\fR, \fBmesh\fR
.IP "\(bu"
Material \fBtype\fR: \fBlambert\fR, \fBphong\fR, \fBblinn_phong\fR, \fBemissive\fR, \fBdielectric\fR
.PP
For \fBmesh\fR geometry with \fBsource = gen(...)\fR, common generators include
\fBplane\fR, \fBcube\fR, \fBicosphere\fR, \fBmenger_sponge\fR, \fBsnowflake\fR, and \fBpyramid\fR.
Mesh modifiers are defined under \fBmodifiers\fR:
\fBrotation\fR, \fBscale\fR, \fBtranslation\fR, \fBflip_normals\fR, \fBextrude\fR.
.PP
Variants can switch camera/material/object wiring:
.PP
.EX
variants = {
  hide_base = true
  night = {
    name = Night
    remove = { object = { fill_light = {} } }
    set = { default_camera = cam_night }
  }
}
.EE
.PP
\fBhide_base\fR only affects the web variant picker visibility for the base option.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Render a scene:
.PP
.EX
\&./build/release/xtracer_cli scene/lab-camera-modes-showcase.scn \\
  -renderer pathtracer_mis -res 1280x720 -samples 4 -aa 2
.EE
.PP
Render with a specific camera and output directory:
.PP
.EX
\&./build/release/xtracer_cli scene/lab-camera-dof-showcase.scn \\
  -cam camera.main -outdir ./renders -renderer pathtracer
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.IP "0"
Success.
.IP "1"
Usage/setup error or scene load failure.
This code is also currently returned by \fBxtracer_cli version\fR.
.IP "2"
Runtime/validation error (for example invalid renderer or camera).
